Contents of tests directories
-----------------------------

conformance
    Non-interactive tests to determine whether an implementation falls within
    the guidelines of OpenGL. It is comprised of two executable: conform and
    conformx.

conformance test development
    Provides a controlled environment for developing new conformance tests.
    Sample templates are included as examples.

coverage
    Non-interactive tests which calls all of the routines with all enumerated
    parameters to insure that all the functions exist and accept the specified
    parameters. It is comprised of three executables: covgl, covglu, covglx,
    corresponding to the the core OpenGL functions, GL Utility functions, and
    GLX, respectively.

primtest
    Non-interactive test of basic primitives with different rendering
    strategies.    

For more information on each test, see the printed documentation or documents
in the doc directory. Also try the -h command-line option for each test.


The script which runs the entire conformance test suite is:

    conform.x - run conform, conformx, covgl, covglu, covglx and primtest.
		Queries for available visuals.

Two useful scripts for debugging or testing are:

    conform.base1 - Runs conform, covgl, covglu and primtest.
		    Queries for available visuals.
    conform.base2 - Runs conform, covgl, covglu and primtest.
		    Assumes 4 standard visuals.
